>> title: Banana Bread
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/banana-bread

Preheat oven to 350F. Grease an #loaf pan{8.5 x 4.5 inch} and line with parchment paper, leaving overhang on the long sides (to lift the bread with).

Add @all-purpose flour{1.5%cups}, @baking soda{1.25%tsp}, and @salt{0.75%tsp} to a #medium bowl{} and #whisk to combine. 

Using an #electric mixer{} on medium-high speed, beat @dark brown sugar{1%cup}, @mascarpone, plain whole-milk Greek yogurt, or sour cream{0.33%cup} and @unsalted butter, room temperature{4%tbsp} in a #large bowl{} until light and fluffy (about ~{4%minutes}). Add @large eggs{2}, one at a time, beating to blend after each addition and scraping down the sides and bottom of the bowl with a #rubber spatula{} as needed.

Reduce speed to low, add dry ingredients, and mix until just combined. 

Add in @large bananas{4}(mashed) and mix until just combined.

Fold @chocolate chips{0.5%cups} into the mixture.

Scrape batter into the prepared loaf pan and smooth the top.

Bake bread until a #tester{} inserted into the center comes out clean (about ~{1%hour}). Transfer pan to a #wire rack{} and let bread cool in the pan for ~{1%hour}. Turn out the bread onto the wire rack and let cool completely (if you can resist) before slicing.